{"idx": 1, "model": "claude-sonnet", "prompt": "p3_analyst_rules", "source": "statements", "orig_row": 1, "gold": 1, "pred": 2, "raw": "Looking at this sentence:\n\n- \"core measures of prices are rising slightly faster than a year ago\" \u2192 hawkish signal (rising inflation)\n- \"continuing rapid advances in productivity have been containing costs and holding down underlying price pressures\" \u2192 dovish signal (falling/contained price pressures)\n\nThe sentence presents both a hawkish element and a dovish counterbalance. The overall message is that despite slightly faster price rises, productivity is keeping underlying pressures contained \u2014 a balanced/mixed picture without a clear directional bias.\n\n**2**", "in_tok": 271, "out_tok": 118, "cost": 0.002583, "error": null}
