{"idx": 121, "model": "claude-sonnet", "prompt": "p3_analyst_rules", "source": "statements", "orig_row": 121, "gold": 2, "pred": 0, "raw": "The sentence describes economic growth that has \"moderated\" (slowed down), a \"cooling of the housing market,\" and \"lagged effects of increases in interest rates and energy prices.\" The overall tone describes a slowing economy with cooling conditions.\n\nThe key signals:\n- \"Moderated\" growth \u2192 economic slowdown\n- \"Cooling of the housing market\" \u2192 economic slack developing\n- These are dovish indicators (economic slowdown, cooling)\n\nHowever, it also mentions \"increases in interest rates and energy prices\" as causes, which are hawkish factors, but they are referenced as past causes, not current pressures.\n\nThe dominant message is economic moderation/cooling, which aligns with dovish signals (economic slack, slowing growth).\n\n**0**", "in_tok": 278, "out_tok": 166, "cost": 0.003324, "error": null}
