{"idx": 827, "model": "claude-sonnet", "prompt": "p3_analyst_rules", "source": "presconf", "orig_row": 310, "gold": 2, "pred": 2, "raw": "Looking at this sentence:\n\n- \"strengthening labor market\" \u2192 hawkish signal (falling unemployment/tightening labor market)\n- \"faster wage growth\" \u2192 hawkish signal (rising wages indicate inflationary pressure)\n- \"2 percent inflation objective\" \u2192 mentions price stability target\n- \"space for wage growth to be higher\" \u2192 suggests current wages are below potential, implying room for accommodation \u2192 dovish lean\n\nThe sentence contains mixed signals: a strengthening labor market (hawkish) but framed with the idea that there's still \"space\" for more wage growth within the inflation objective (dovish/accommodative framing). The overall tone is balanced \u2014 acknowledging labor market strength while suggesting wages can still rise without breaching inflation targets.\n\n**2**", "in_tok": 287, "out_tok": 168, "cost": 0.003381, "error": null}
