{"idx": 1740, "model": "claude-sonnet", "prompt": "p3_analyst_rules", "source": "presconf", "orig_row": 814, "gold": 2, "pred": 2, "raw": "The sentence reports payroll growth running at a \"sub-4 percent pace,\" which suggests slowing/moderate growth. This is reported as a factual observation without a clear directional bias toward tightening or easing. The term \"sub-4 percent\" implies moderation, which leans neutral/dovish, but since it's reported as a data point without explicit directional commentary, the neutral classification applies.\n\n**2**", "in_tok": 267, "out_tok": 95, "cost": 0.002226, "error": null}
{"idx": 1748, "model": "claude-sonnet", "prompt": "p3_analyst_rules", "source": "presconf", "orig_row": 822, "gold": 0, "pred": 1, "raw": "The sentence reports core PCE inflation running at 1.9 percent \u2014 very close to but slightly below the 2% target. This is a factual report of an economic variable without a clear directional bias (neither explicitly rising nor falling, just \"running at\" a level). Per the annotation rules, when data is reported without clear directional bias, prefer Neutral.\n\n**2**", "in_tok": 266, "out_tok": 85, "cost": 0.002073, "error": null}
